        origin        derived;
        method        "Clausius-Clapeyron interpolation (ln P linear in 1/T) between two measured boiling points: 1/Tb = 1/T1 + [ln(101.325/P1) / ln(P2/P1)] * (1/T2 - 1/T1), with (T1, P1) = (406.8 K, 100 kPa) and (T2, P2) = (413.1 K, 120 kPa); ln(101.325/100) = 0.0131630, ln(120/100) = 0.1823216, 1/T1 = 0.00245821 1/K, 1/T2 = 0.00242072 1/K, so 1/Tb = 0.00245550 1/K and Tb = 407.248 K, rounded to 407.25 K; the archive holds no measurement AT 101.325 kPa for this substance, and the ChemSep value it REPLACES (404.15 K) lies below the 100 kPa measurement (406.8 K), so it is contradicted";
        inputs
